// CROWN — a callback RETURNED uncalled performs nothing in make's
// evaluation: f's cell is no terminal of make's body row (abstraction is
// pure), so `!E` gates nothing and the performing callback is admitted —
// the crown's latent/performed rule. Expect NO E_EffectMismatch.
effect E { op() -> Int }
handler h { op() => resume(7) }
fn make(f) with !E = () => f()
fn main() = ((make(() => op()))()) ~> h
